    body: `
<p>Shopping puts together three things you already know: question words, classifiers and describers after the noun. This lesson adds the words for clothes, colors and paying.</p>
<h3>How much?</h3>
<p><b>ราคาเท่าไร</b> <i>raa-khaa thâo-rai</i> asks the price; you will often hear <b>เท่าไหร่</b>. Point at the item with noun + classifier + <b>นี้</b>.</p>
{{ex:เสื้อตัวนี้ราคาเท่าไร|sûuea dtuua níi raa-khaa thâo-rai|How much is this shirt?}}
<p>At markets, polite bargaining is normal; in malls and shops with price tags it is not. Ask with a smile:</p>
{{ex:ลดได้ไหม|lót dâai mǎi|Can you lower the price?}}
<h3>Clothes and their classifiers</h3>
<p>Each kind of thing has its classifier. English counts pants as "a pair"; Thai counts them like shirts, with <b>ตัว</b> <i>dtuua</i>. Shoes really come in pairs: <b>คู่</b> <i>khûu</i>.</p>
<div class="tbl"><table><tr><th>Thing</th><th>Thai</th><th>Classifier</th></tr><tr><td>shirt</td><td class="k">เสื้อ</td><td class="k">ตัว</td></tr><tr><td>pants</td><td class="k">กางเกง</td><td class="k">ตัว</td></tr><tr><td>skirt</td><td class="k">กระโปรง</td><td class="k">ตัว</td></tr><tr><td>shoes</td><td class="k">รองเท้า</td><td class="k">คู่</td></tr><tr><td>hat, bag</td><td class="k">หมวก, กระเป๋า</td><td class="k">ใบ</td></tr></table></div>
{{ex:รองเท้าคู่นี้|raawng-tháao khûu níi|this pair of shoes}}
<h3>Colors after the noun</h3>
<p>A color is a describer, so it comes after the noun, with <b>สี</b> <i>sǐi</i> (color) in front. With a classifier, the order is noun, color, classifier, นี้.</p>
{{ex:เสื้อสีแดง|sûuea sǐi daaeng|a red shirt}}
{{ex:กางเกงสีดำตัวนี้|gaang-geeng sǐi dam dtuua níi|these black pants}}
<h3>Trying on: too big, too small</h3>
<p><b>ลองได้ไหม</b> asks "can I try it on?". After a describing word, <b>ไป</b> <i>bpai</i> means "too": <b>ใหญ่ไป</b> is too big, <b>แพงไป</b> too expensive.</p>
{{ex:ลองได้ไหม|laawng dâai mǎi|Can I try it on?}}
{{ex:แพงไป|phaaeng bpai|too expensive}}
<p>Careful with <b>ฟิต</b> <i>fít</i>: it does not mean "fits well". It means tight.</p>
{{ex:กางเกงตัวนี้ฟิต|gaang-geeng dtuua níi fít|These pants are too tight.}}
<h3>Paying</h3>
<p>Most shops and many stalls take QR payment from a banking app; you can also pay in cash, <b>เงินสด</b> <i>ngoen-sòt</i>. If you are only browsing, <b>ดูก่อน</b> ("look first") with ครับ or ค่ะ tells the seller you are just looking.</p>
{{ex:สแกนได้ไหม|sà-gaaen dâai mǎi|Can I pay by QR code?}}
<div class="tip"><b>Most common mistake:</b> the color in front, as in English. <b>สีแดงเสื้อ</b> → <b>เสื้อสีแดง</b>. The noun comes first, then สี and the color.</div>
`,
